    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0668" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.51/213.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Minister.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-01-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Advises him that the British Foreign Office seems to be better disposed toward
                    the Guatemala loan agreement. The Department would deplore it if the Guatemalan
                    Government should send a special agent to London, as that might furnish a
                    possible excuse for delay.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
